{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336731-how-could-one-go-about-playing-an-ancient-dreamspeaker","id":1336731,"title":"How could one go about playing an ancient Dreamspeaker?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-18T18:41:39-07:00","id":1336731,"title":"How could one go about playing an ancient Dreamspeaker?","content":"Greetings.<br /> <br /> I find that ancient religions such as the Canaanite or the Ancient Sumerian religion have plenty of animistic aspects to them, and their priests were considered intermediaries between the gods and various spirits. How difficult would it be to play a Dreamspeaker who subscribed to some ancient religion of this sort, primarily from a logistics perspective? For example, finding tools/foci to channel their deities, having other worshipers of their archaic beliefs to support them, summoning spirits, etc. Information about belief systems during the Iron and Bronze ages is scarce to come by, too. How could one make it work?<br /> <br /> To specify: I\u2019m talking about playing them in a modern context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","user":"KingJohn","date":". 09-19-2019, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T19:28:25-07:00","id":1336743,"title":"","content":"The same way modern shamans practice their craft. Really nothing has changed over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T20:14:07-07:00","id":1336751,"title":"","content":"But surely there\u2019s a difference between modern shaman vs 2,000 years ago ancient practices?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T21:12:32-07:00","id":1336764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336731-how-could-one-go-about-playing-an-ancient-dreamspeaker?p=1336751#post1336751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But surely there\u2019s a difference between modern shaman vs 2,000 years ago ancient practices?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is baking a loaf of bread in an earth oven any different then baking one in a modern one? Sure the tools might have changed but your still baking bread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T22:37:18-07:00","id":1336774,"title":"","content":"I suppose I\u2019m asking how would Dreamspeakers living in modern times practice ancient religions/shamanic practices?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T22:41:22-07:00","id":1336775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336731-how-could-one-go-about-playing-an-ancient-dreamspeaker?p=1336774#post1336774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I\u2019m asking how would Dreamspeakers living in modern times practice ancient religions/shamanic practices?</div> </div> </div> </div>By practicing the ancient religion and shamanic practices. Using their tools and rituals. Maybe not so much living as they did by throwing off the trappings of modern civilization but at knowing the mindset","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T07:27:43-07:00","id":1336864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, finding tools/foci to channel their deities, having other worshipers of their archaic beliefs to support them, summoning spirits, etc. Information about belief systems during the Iron and Bronze ages is scarce to come by, too. How could one make it work?</div> </div> </div> </div>tools/foci : If the ancients were able to craft these, you can be sure that modern people can do it too. Depending on how traditionalist you are, employing modern methods may be ok for you or not. If you don't like to use modern methods, there's astoundingly big subcultures that are all about crafting stuff using older methods (you can find videos about crafting stuff with bronze age technology on youtube). And most likely you're initiated in such a subculture or know someone who is, if you're a Dreamspeaker. You should be able to learn the necessary skills and get the materials to craft foci in the traditional way w/o problem.<br /> <br /> Information: Books, talking with people who knows (historians, archeologists, descendants of the people that have an oral tradition, spirits that literally were there).<br /> The Internet can be a place to start building your contacts and finding works about the subject, if you don't have anything better. However, being that you're a Dreamspeaker you could/should take advantage of the knowledge sources of your peers. Most likely you're not the only shaman who believes in whatever you believe, the others can give you a place to start.<br /> <br /> Usually this manifests trough Backgrounds that represent the people that help you getting what you need (like Mentor or Allies) and Abilities that help you do your thing (like Esoterica, Crafts, Art).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-19-2019, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T07:57:08-07:00","id":1336869,"title":"","content":"No one looks up one day and decides, &quot;Hey, I'm going to start believing in a bunch of ancient shamanistic practices. I guess I better go down to the library and figure out what they are.&quot; At least some familiarity with the subject matter has to come first, whether that is learned from a mentor, a patron, or some other source. What I'm trying to say is that your backstory, whatever it is, should already establish your baseline knowledge with an otherwise esoteric field of knowledge. That doesn't mean your character is done learning, just that they have enough to function while they search for more.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for inspiration for how they got that baseline knowledge in the first place, the big three I can think of are: taught by an already practicing mentor, taught by a Spirit with ties to that era, and started with a single working wonder (to provide the basis for their belief) and did a lot of trial and error with what research they were able to do.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}